{%- comment -%}
  Discrete cookie banner. Accept/Reject only — no dark patterns, no
  pre-ticked choice. js/emoti-consent.js stores the decision in
  localStorage and only THEN (and only on Accept) loads the Meta Pixel,
  using settings.meta_pixel_id (blank by default — see Theme settings →
  Tracking & consent).

  This is a minimal, honest CMP. If you later install a dedicated consent
  platform (e.g. one of the Shopify App Store CMPs, or Cookiebot), replace
  this snippet's markup/logic with that tool's embed and keep
  window.EMOTI_CONSENT as the single source of truth the Pixel loader
  reads — the rest of assets/emoti-consent.js does not need to change.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="cookie-banner" id="cookie-banner" role="dialog" aria-label="Cookie preferences" hidden>
  <p>{{ 'emoti.cookie.text' | t }}</p>
  <div class="cookie-banner__actions">
    <button type="button" id="cookie-reject">{{ 'emoti.cookie.reject' | t }}</button>
    <button type="button" id="cookie-accept">{{ 'emoti.cookie.accept' | t }}</button>
  </div>
</div>
